    "media:imagetext": "Normally\nthe\ncrew\nwill\nexits for you,\nopen\nthe\nwhen required in an\nemergency, but the method of open-\ning each is shown here.\nWindow Exits in position A\nLift flap and pull handle\ndown\nwindow will fall outwards.\nDoor exits in position B\nPull handle out and down.\ndoor open.\nPush\nWe do everything we can to make\nyour flight as free from restrictions\nas possible.\nAt the same time,\nfor\nyour comfort and well-being,\nthere\nare certain instructions we must ask\nyou to read and note.\nWe hope the\nfollowing guidance\nboth\nunderstand\nwill help you\nthese\nrules\nand\nappreciate the need for them.\nIf you\nhave any questions or problems, your\nhostesses are always on hand to give\nhelp.\nQUICK RELEASE\nDuring Take-off and Landing\nOn boarding the aircraft, all hand\nbaggage must be placed under the\nseat and kept there during\nthe\nflight). The overhead rack is for hats\nand coats only.\nSmoking is not permitted during\ntake-off or landing,\nand when the\nNo Smoking' signs are illuminated,\nor at any time in the toilets.\nPortable radios\nMust not be used during your flight\nas this could interfere with the elec-\ntronic equipment of the aircraft.\nSeat-belts must be fastened for take-\noff\nand\nlanding,\nwhenever\nthe\nFasten Seat Belt' sign is illuminated,\nor when instructed by a member of\nthe crew. (Note the method of quick\nrelease).\nEmergency Exits\nPlease note\nthe\nposition\nof\nthe\nEmergency Exits, as shown on this\ndiagram.",
